    @* ============================== Feature grid ============================== *@

    <section class="bb-section">
        <p class="bb-overline">Capabilities</p>
        <h2>A scanner component, and the decoder behind it</h2>
        <p class="bb-section-sub">
            <code>&lt;BbScanner&gt;</code> owns the camera, the frame loop, the overlays and the controls;
            <code>BbBarcodeDecoder</code> turns pixels into a strongly typed <code>BbBarcodeResult</code> - with
            the corner points, the raw bytes and the symbol's metadata - wherever .NET runs.
        </p>
        <div class="bb-grid">
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-primary"></span> Every parameter, live</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">
                    Formats, frame rate, processing size, region, duplicate suppression and the advanced
                    <code>BbScannerOptions</code> - all applied to the running camera without dropping it.
                </p>
                <a href="scan" class="btn btn-outline">Live playground →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-success"></span> Camera, torch and zoom</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">
                    Device selection, front and rear cameras, torch and zoom where the hardware offers them -
                    and never a control the hardware will refuse.
                </p>
                <a href="camera" class="btn btn-outline">Camera control →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-warning"></span> Aim with a region</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">
                    A normalized <code>BbScanRegion</code> crops the frame before any pixel is touched, so every
                    later stage gets cheaper in proportion to the area removed.
                </p>
                <a href="region" class="btn btn-outline">Scan region →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-danger"></span> Photos and buffers</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">
                    A built-in file picker and drop target for still images, <code>ScanImageAsync</code> for an
                    upload the application already holds, and <code>DecodeImage</code> for raw pixels - tuned for
                    one exhaustive attempt rather than fifteen a second, and never asking for the camera.
                </p>
                <a href="image" class="btn btn-outline">Image scanning →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-warning"></span> Built for real workflows</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">
                    Read one code and stop, pause for "scan another", count each value once for a stocktake, ignore
                    every code but the one you expect, read a whole sheet of labels at once, and beep or vibrate on a scan.
                </p>
                <a href="lifecycle" class="btn btn-outline">Lifecycle &amp; duplicates →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-primary"></span> Measured, not guessed</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">
                    Per-stage timings for every frame, and a decoder benchmark that runs in your browser on your
                    device - with no garbage allocated per frame.
                </p>
                <a href="performance" class="btn btn-outline">Performance →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-success"></span> Yours to restyle and translate</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">
                    Every colour, radius and dimension is a CSS custom property, the reticle and the messages are
                    render fragments, and every text it shows or announces can be translated - with right-to-left,
                    screen readers, reduced motion and forced colours built in.
                </p>
                <a href="customize" class="btn btn-outline">Customisation →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-danger"></span> Failures you can act on</h3>
